*Normal Mounting**
1. First check which disk is available for mounting ---> $ sudo lsblk or fdisk -l (for full details)

2. Then mount that on mount point ---> $ sudo mount -t ext4 /dev/sdb /var/log/nginx (Paths can be different) if mounted then no need to format.
And if not mounted then we need to format first and confirm with seniors

3. For format the file System's partition ---> $ sudo mkfs -t ext4 /dev/sdb (Paths can be different)

4. For making permanent that partition by entering the entry in /etc/fstab file
like that ---> $ sudo vim /etc/fstab >>>

>——————> “UUID <dest_dir> <file_type> <options> <dump> <pass>" (Paths can be different) this is for requirement basis entry
e.g.:-
(i). UUID /var/log/nginx ext4 defaults,_netdev,noatime,barrier=0 0 0

5. for finding UUID ---> $ sudo blkid

6. Now check ---> $ df -hT or df -h

